Reuse the echo canceller's filter from before recording started again, and its ERLE

Patches 0010 and 0014 align AEC3 again when recording starts again in a call (a
microphone turned on again, or the audio device restarting by itself for an output
changed): the render buffer and delay estimator start over, and so do both linear
filters and the ERLE (kBufferFlush with recording_restarted; the transparent mode is
kept). The room has not changed, only the alignment, but AEC3 takes its filters for
unconverged again (their adaptation, its filter quality) and starts its ERLE over, and
meanwhile it suppresses by its nonlinear estimate. Measured in the call
lab against the same call with no change: a word said in double talk in the seconds
after an output change or an unmute loses 5.3 dB at 0.5 s and 1.9 dB at 3.5 s, and the
other side's echo comes back in bursts in 4 of 16 changes.

Now, at that restart (recording_restarted: not the restart for other devices of patch
0016, which forgets the transparent mode and may be another room) the subtractor keeps
its refined filter (GetFilter()) and its size (SizePartitions()), and the AEC state its
ERLE (Erle(false), Erle(true), ErleUnbounded()), before resetting them as before. Any
other flush of the render buffer (kBufferFlush without a restart: a render overrun, the
restart for other devices) forgets both. A restart again while they are kept and no
reused filter is in use (0015's two realigns a few ms apart) keeps the ones from before
the first, as the filters and ERLE then were just reset; its window starts again.

At each new delay found (kNewDetectedDelay) within kReuseWindowBlocks of the restart
while no reused filter is in use, the filters are reset as before and the saved one is
tried, shifted by -kReuseMaxShiftPartitions to +kReuseMaxShiftPartitions partitions
(partition p taking partition p + shift; the delay estimator puts the echo at the same
partition after the restart, so no shift is the expected one), over the next
kReuseTrialBlocks blocks whose capture is over kReuseMinTrialPower (y2 summed over the
capture channels); a trial still running when the window closes ends there. Each
candidate's output s is compared with the capture y, each
capture channel with its gain sy/ss clamped to [-kReuseMaxTrialGain,
kReuseMaxTrialGain], and the one leaving the least (e2/y2, e2 = yy - 2 g sy + g^2 ss) is
put in both filters, scaled by its gain, if that residual is under kReuseMaxResidual
and every channel's gain is within [1/kReuseMaxGain, kReuseMaxGain]; the log says
"AEC3: filter from before recording started again reused" with the shift, gain,
residual and how long after the restart. A new delay during the trial starts it over;
a trial that fails leaves the filters as they adapted meanwhile, and the next new delay
in the window tries again.

While the reused filter is in use (Subtractor::FilterReusedAfterRestart, told to the
AEC state after each block's subtraction and to the block processor through the echo
remover):
- a new delay at most kReuseMaxShiftPartitions blocks from the one before shifts both
  filters by the blocks the render buffer moved (EchoPathVariability::
  delay_change_blocks, new) instead of resetting them; a larger one, or any flush, ends
  the reuse and resets them as before (the AEC state resets as before at every delay
  change, the ERLE estimator with it);
- for its first kReuseWindowBlocks blocks, the block processor does not align to an
  estimate within one block of the one it aligned to, taking it as the estimator's
  jitter;
- out of the transparent mode, the linear estimate is usable and the linear output used
  (UsableLinearEstimate, UseLinearFilterOutput), as once a filter has converged;
- on the blocks where the linear output keeps at most half of the capture (E2 <=
  0.5 Y2 summed over the bands), y2 and e2 are summed per band with a forgetting factor
  of 0.98; from 5 such blocks on, Erle(false), Erle(true) and ErleUnbounded() return
  max(the estimator's, min(the one saved at the restart, y2/e2)) per band. The
  unbounded one goes, as upstream, through the residual echo estimator's
  LinearEstimate to R2_unbounded and the suppressor's dominant nearend detector; the
  values stay over the estimator's, so positive.
The reuse lasts until a reset of the filters ends it. The saved filter is forgotten
kReuseWindowBlocks after the restart unless a reuse is in use.

AdaptiveFirFilter::SetSizePartitions now does nothing when asked, without immediate
effect, for the size the filter already has and is not changing (the initial state's
end asking the reused filter for the size it was given at once).

Left alone: a call's start and an echo controller made anew, the restart for other
devices (0016), the transparent mode (kept as 0010 keeps it), the delay estimator, the
suppressor's and residual echo's models, any delay change while no filter is reused, and
the refined filter's gain state (it starts over at the reset as before, also for the
reused filter). All of it runs on the capture thread, in the block processor's capture
call. No test reaches it: none restarts recording.

Constants (Subtractor): kReuseWindowBlocks 2500 (10 s), kReuseMaxShiftPartitions 8,
kReuseTrialBlocks 25, kReuseMinTrialPower 50^2 * 64, kReuseMaxResidual 0.5,
kReuseMaxTrialGain 4, kReuseMaxGain 1.41; in the AEC state: 0.5 (E2/Y2), 0.98 and 5
blocks.

Measured: not yet.

